# IIQ AngularJS + XHTML Naming Conventions

## Files

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| JS controller | PascalCase + `Ctrl` suffix | `CertScheduleCtrl.js` |
| JS directive | camelCase, `sp` prefix for shared | `spDatePicker.js`, `columnDataDirective.js` |
| JS service | PascalCase + `Service` suffix | `DateValidationService.js` |
| JS filter | PascalCase + `Filter` suffix | `DateFormatFilter.js` |
| XHTML page | camelCase | `certificationSchedule.xhtml` |
| Test file | Mirrors source + `Tests` suffix | `DateValidationServiceTests.js` |

## AngularJS elements

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Directive name | camelCase, `sp` prefix for shared | `spDatePicker`, `spColumnData` |
| Directive in HTML | kebab-case | `<sp-date-picker>`, `sp-column-data` |
| Controller | PascalCase + `Ctrl` | `CertScheduleCtrl` |
| Service/factory | PascalCase + `Service` | `DateValidationService` |
| Filter | camelCase | `dateFormat` |
| Scope variable | camelCase | `$scope.startDate`, `$scope.isValid` |
| Scope function | camelCase, verb-first | `$scope.submitForm()`, `$scope.validateDate()` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`, `DATE_FORMAT_ISO` |
| Events | colon-separated namespace | `certification:dateChanged`, `modal:closed` |

## Message Keys (iiqMessages.properties)

Format: `ui_{feature}_{component}_{action}`

```
ui_cert_schedule_title=Certification Schedule
ui_cert_schedule_save_success=Schedule saved successfully
ui_cert_schedule_error_invalid_date=Please enter a valid date
ui_common_datepicker_placeholder=Select a date
```

Used by: AngularJS templates (`{{ 'ui_cert_schedule_title' | translate }}`), XHTML pages (`<h:outputText value="#{msgs.ui_cert_schedule_title}"/>`), Java resources (via `MessageCatalog.get("ui_cert_schedule_title")`).

**Never** put dynamic data (entitlement lists, application lists, per-tenant content) into this file — those come from REST/DB.
